# Decap CMS — agent-maintained content

The user expects the agent to **update site content** on request. Do this by editing the Markdown/YAML
files under `src/content/` and media under `public/uploads/` — the same files Decap CMS manages
at `/admin/`.

## Workflow

1. Read the relevant collection schema in `src/content.config.ts` and matching fields in
   `public/admin/config.yml`.
2. Edit content in `src/content/<collection>/de/` (and `public/uploads/` for new media).
3. Match existing frontmatter field names exactly — parity is enforced by `tests/unit/cms-config-parity.test.ts`.
4. Commit and push to `main` when the user wants it live (triggers GitHub Actions deploy).

## Collections (CMS labels → folder)

| CMS section | Content path |
| --- | --- |
| Website-Texte | `src/content/site/de/index.md` |
| Vita | `src/content/biography/de/index.md` |
| Projekte | `src/content/projects/de/*.md` |
| Programme | `src/content/programs/de/*.md` |
| Termine | `src/content/tour-dates/de/*.md` |
| CDs | `src/content/discography/de/*.md` |
| Unterricht | `src/content/teaching/de/index.md` |
| Kontakt | `src/content/contact/de/index.md` |
| Rechtliches | `src/content/legal/de/*.md` |

## DecapBridge / git-gateway

Production auth uses DecapBridge (`public/admin/config.yml`). The agent does not log into `/admin/`
— it writes content files directly, which is equivalent to a CMS publish after push.

Auth setup reference: `docs/cms-auth-setup.md`. Change `backend.*` credentials only when setting up
a new deployment or when the user asks.
